{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "Immediate-release tablet: excipient blend and compression force",
  "notes": "Direct-compression tablet, 400 mg, with 14 % w/w API and 1 % w/w magnesium stearate held constant; the remaining 85 % w/w is split between microcrystalline cellulose (filler), povidone K30 (binder) and croscarmellose sodium (disintegrant). Each blend was compressed on a single-station instrumented press at the planned force. Room relative humidity was logged during compression because the binder and the disintegrant are hygroscopic. Hardness is the mean of 10 tablets, disintegration time the slowest of 6 tablets (Ph. Eur. 2.9.1, water, 37 °C) and dissolution the mean of 6 vessels (USP II, 50 rpm, pH 6.8). Quality targets: hardness at least 80 N, disintegration below 3 min, dissolution at 30 min near 90 % (not below 80 %).",
